               </eventList>
               <p xml:id="idm101">The little overture was written for a New Year's Eve entertainment in Studenterforeningen (The Students' Society). The title refers to Gade's own overture "Echoes of Ossian", which had had its first performance on 19 November 1841. In the overture Gade cites three different tunes: the national anthem of the Danish kings "Kong Christian stod ved højen Mast", the Austrian folk song "Ach du lieber Augustin", which had become known in Denmark in connection with the publishing of Hans Christian Andersen's tale "Svinedrengen" (The Swineherd) on 20 december 1841, and Rudolph Bay's "Smilende Haab" (Smiling Hope).</p>
            </history>
